<title>GERMANY: Opel says teams with Renault, Suzuki on vehicles.</title>
<headline>Opel says teams with Renault, Suzuki on vehicles.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adam Opel AG, a unit of General Motors Corp, said on Thursday it has teamed up with French carmaker Renault to build light trucks that will be introduced into the market at the turn of the century.</p>
<p>Opel said the trucks will be in the 2.5 tonne to 2.8 tonne weight class. The long-term deal was signed within the last six weeks, Opel chief executive David Herman said in a statement issued at the carmaker's annual news conference.</p>
<p>Opel also said it was reviewing a possible joint venture with Japan's Suzuki Motor Corp for the production of vehicles in the small car segment.</p>
<p>--John Gilardi, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
